{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits","id":1082873,"title":"Using Fate on Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-23T19:28:10-07:00","id":1082873,"title":"Using Fate on Spirits","content":"So I'm putting our cabal's Acanthus against a storm spirit. Their battle is on a rooftop amidst a typhoom battering the city. Are spirits vulnerable to Fate magic? Are they affected by Boons and Hexes, and do they have Sympathetic links as well? <br /> <br /> This could be a silly question, but I'd love to hear your thoughts. The Acanthus has Spirit 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T20:47:49-07:00","id":1082886,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that Spirits are subject to Fate spells per the normal rules. Since I didn't saw any rule dictating otherwise.<br /> But I think that some spirits can't be affect by some Conditions and Tilts(Hexes), like, you can't blind a spirit that does not need to see.<br /> <br /> As per the Sympathetic Links. I also think that this rules apply normally. On the Fallen World Chronicles there is a strange Tree that has multiple destinies attached to it and a spirit habitating it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T00:21:29-07:00","id":1082926,"title":"","content":"Yep, feel free to hex away and exploit sympathies. Keep in mind though that the spirit's ban and bane probably trump any curse on it telling it to act contrary against it. No official rules on it AFAIK, but I'd say that either the curse flat-out fails, or the spirit goes overloaded on lowercase-p paradox and goes berserk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T04:45:18-07:00","id":1082968,"title":"","content":"Nah. The bane simply damages the spirit. It should be possible (though extremely unlikely to the point where it basically never happens) for the spirit to approach a bane on their own.<br /> Bans are also not that bad. Many bans have consequences for failing to uphold a ban, and it's mentioned that forcing an ephemeral to go against their ban is an Act of Hubris against Enlightened and Understanding Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-24-2017, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T05:19:15-07:00","id":1082976,"title":"","content":"As long as you spend a reach to add spirit, I dot see why it wouldn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T05:48:13-07:00","id":1082982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1082976#post1082976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as you spend a reach to add spirit, I dot see why it wouldn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to spend reach to make Fate able to affect them, you do need to be able to perceive spirits though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T06:01:47-07:00","id":1082985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1082982#post1082982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need to spend reach to make Fate able to affect them, you do need to be able to perceive spirits though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or cast area affecting spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:00:13-07:00","id":1083036,"title":"","content":"I would assume Fate would work fine on spirits for just the same reason that Mind spells also do (despite my kinda sorta grudge against that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:25:54-07:00","id":1083048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1083036#post1083036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would assume Fate would work fine on spirits for just the same reason that Mind spells also do (despite my kinda sorta grudge against that).</div> </div> </div> </div>I also agree that mind to control spirits is abit Meh, but at least the withstand rating for mind is resistance for a spirit and not just rank its rank..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:30:33-07:00","id":1083050,"title":"","content":"They still Withstand with Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:58:13-07:00","id":1083063,"title":"","content":"Mind can work on spirits because they have a conscious(ish) mind that mind magic can naturally detect. I would think that with Fate magic, unless the spirit materializes in front of your, you would need a couple of dots in Spirit to be able to target it. I don't see how fate would specifically locate the spirit otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T12:36:08-07:00","id":1083140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1083063#post1083063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind can work on spirits because they have a conscious(ish) mind that mind magic can naturally detect. I would think that with Fate magic, unless the spirit materializes in front of your, you would need a couple of dots in Spirit to be able to target it. I don't see how fate would specifically locate the spirit otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind AoE doesn't target spirits because spirits have minds that the spell can detect and home in on. All AoE spells (regardless of Arcanum used) simply affects everything inside a targeted area (if it can be affected by that spell at all). Whether or not you can personally perceive those who area doesn't matter. A spirit in Twilight is still very much there. It's physically intangible, but that doesn't affect the spell's ability to target you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-24-2017, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:21:29-07:00","id":1083177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1083050#post1083050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They still Withstand with Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>even tho is says for psychic dominate resolve?, doesnt it then transfer to the spirits resistance, just like if it was stamina id be power? They get -1 dicepool to try bind a spirit via rank? Ive had this argument with my players in 1e, is mind controlling a spirit binding it? I said yes because theres no official &quot;bind&quot; term in mage and your using mind to &quot;bind&quot; it to your will?<br /> <br /> #edit nvm saw it in the book....fuck sake, mind is still OP, get mind 2 first then work on seeing ghosts/spirits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-24-2017, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:32:12-07:00","id":1083184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1083140#post1083140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind AoE doesn't target spirits because spirits have minds that the spell can detect and home in on. All AoE spells (regardless of Arcanum used) simply affects everything inside a targeted area (if it can be affected by that spell at all). Whether or not you can personally perceive those who area doesn't matter. A spirit in Twilight is still very much there. It's physically intangible, but that doesn't affect the spell's ability to target you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So an astrally projecting vampire and an angel lurking in twilight would both be hexed in the area too? My understanding of the defensive value of the twilight state takes another hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T15:01:13-07:00","id":1083196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1083184#post1083184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So an astrally projecting vampire and an angel lurking in twilight would both be hexed in the area too? My understanding of the defensive value of the twilight state takes another hit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, they would also be affected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T15:15:19-07:00","id":1083201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1083184#post1083184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So an astrally projecting vampire and an angel lurking in twilight would both be hexed in the area too? My understanding of the defensive value of the twilight state takes another hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, how often to mages target AoE? If they want to cast an offensive spell they're often better off targeting subjects since they don't want to catch themselves or their allies in the effect, nor have their opponents just run out from the affected area. The only time I've ever seen AoE being used has been with Co-Location since you'd want a portal large enough to at least climb through.<br /> And if the rarity of AoE spells holds true in other groups as well the angel has a huge defensive advantage in not being visible to neither of the Twilight revealing two dot Attainments. If you can't perceive it you can't cast a spell directly on it, and even if you do cast AoE spells you can't be sure the angel is in the affected area.<br /> Vampires also have a defensive advantage in that they're just projecting. There's no explicit rules, but the projection would most likely use the dream form rules, just like the Mind spell Psychic Projection (sans being able to use any mystical powers). That means if the projection is killed the vampire would just wake up with Soul Shocked. And some STs might rule that any spells cast on the projection would cancel once the vampire wakes up since it was the projection that was the subject; not the actual vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T19:55:07-07:00","id":1084828,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all the interesting ideas and perspectives! This is what's great about this forum. I'll post an update after our next session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T00:55:50-07:00","id":1084921,"title":"","content":"Something worth noting about Spirits, is that it's frequently a very bad idea to try and affect them with Withstood spells from outside of their &quot;native&quot; Arcanum.<br /> Spirits withstand most other spells (which brush up against Stamina, Composure or Resolve), with Resistance.<br /> <br /> This is both more flexible for Spirits, and has a higher cap that its Rank.<br /> A Rank 3 Spirit can have a Resistance as high as 9, meaning a Mage will have to pump his Potency up to 10, or pray for an Exceptional Success to affect it.<br /> Meanwhile a Spirit mage can reliably expect its Withstand to be 3.<br /> <br /> This advice is similarly pertinent for Ephemeral Entities other than Spirits, but you're unlikely to run into too many Rank 3-4 Ghosts or Goetia in your day to day life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T01:01:33-07:00","id":1084922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1084921#post1084921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something worth noting about Spirits, is that it's frequently a very bad idea to try and affect them with Withstood spells from outside of their &quot;native&quot; Arcanum.<br /> Spirits withstand most other spells (which brush up against Stamina, Composure or Resolve), with Resistance.<br /> <br /> This is both more flexible for Spirits, and has a higher cap that its Rank.<br /> A Rank 3 Spirit can have a Resistance as high as 9, meaning a Mage will have to pump his Potency up to 10, or pray for an Exceptional Success to affect it.<br /> Meanwhile a Spirit mage can reliably expect its Withstand to be 3.<br /> <br /> This advice is similarly pertinent for Ephemeral Entities other than Spirits, but you're unlikely to run into too many Rank 3-4 Ghosts or Goetia in your day to day life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually as i found out recently (in this thread in fact) ALL ephermeral entitities withstand ALL spells with rank. It put a bit of a downer on my plans for a rank 4 spirit bad guy, who can now be abused like a sock puppet by anybody with spirit 3 or mind 3<br /> <br /> p127 under determine withstand trait step.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">. Living (or undead) subjects usually Withstand spells with<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Stamina (for physical transformations or afflictions), Resolve<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">(for attempted mind control or other mental effects), or Composure (for emotional manipulation or effects that target sanity,<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">perception, or the soul). Ephemeral entities Withstand spells<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">with their Rank.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-28-2017, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T01:19:39-07:00","id":1084926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1084922#post1084922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually as i found out recently (in this thread in fact) ALL ephermeral entitities withstand ALL spells with rank. It put a bit of a downer on my plans for a rank 4 spirit bad guy, who can now be abused like a sock puppet by anybody with spirit 3 or mind 3<br /> <br /> p127 under determine withstand trait step.</div> </div> </div> </div>Houserule it otherwise? Let rank only be a matter in spells that actually are normally supposed to involve such entities - and things that effect all entities use resistance? Or, if you want to play without using a house rule to call it otherwise, use something like a claimed. I mean, its one think to withstand something with a withstand of 4 because that's it's rank - but once it becomes a claimed it's a) no longer ephemeral and b) spreading it's resistance traits to it's host, making it's host likely have much higher traits than it's native rank <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or, create a custom ephemeral entity which has no rank - mages in twilight still use their attributes, so a creature that uses those attributes that somehow became ephemeral would work. Or, create a Numina which allows an entity to use their Resistance as Withstand. Your options are limitless!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T01:36:47-07:00","id":1084928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082873-using-fate-on-spirits?p=1084926#post1084926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Houserule it otherwise? Let rank only be a matter in spells that actually are normally supposed to involve such entities - and things that effect all entities use resistance? Or, if you want to play without using a house rule to call it otherwise, use something like a claimed. I mean, its one think to withstand something with a withstand of 4 because that's it's rank - but once it becomes a claimed it's a) no longer ephemeral and b) spreading it's resistance traits to it's host, making it's host likely have much higher traits than it's native rank <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Or, create a custom ephemeral entity which has no rank - mages in twilight still use their attributes, so a creature that uses those attributes that somehow became ephemeral would work. Or, create a Numina which allows an entity to use their Resistance as Withstand. Your options are limitless!</div> </div> </div> </div>In the 1e game i ran the spirit eventually bonded with a vampire who had Blood Tenebrous 5 from the book of spirits (wasnt as cheesy as it sounds, it was a abyss spirit from the prince of 100,000 reality so i assumed they would have vampire puppet bodies in that realm as standard and it managed to trick the playes into summoning its &quot;body&quot; when they were tying to get get rid of it), it was pretty OP then but still got its ass handed to it via white phos grenades. Im thinking of converting my 1e game that lasted years to 2e for new players as i cant be arsed coming up with something new atm..<br /> <br /> But yeh a claimed is probably an idea, all you then have to worry about is mind 2/3 :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-28-2017, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T01:46:32-07:00","id":1084929,"title":"","content":"Well I mean... even the mind 2/3 isn't a big worry when your resolve/composure suddenly goes up by ... however many dots you raise it by (rank 4? I'd give them +3/4 depending on the spirit type. Or rather, it's not as -big- a worry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}